# What is ignored, and -- more importantly -- what is deliberately not.

### Build output ###
# The Haskell prototype's build tree (redirected under a cache in CI and reaper,
# but it lands here on a workstation).
/proto/dist-newstyle/
# Cabal's own store when CI redirects CABAL_DIR into the clone.
/.cabal_cache/
# Rust workspace output, from Phase 1 on.
/target/
/dist/
/.cargo_cache/
# The wine prefix the CI Windows test step creates.
/.wine/
# Python's bytecode cache, written beside any module that is imported: the
# Python SDK, the tenants' hook fixtures. Build output, never source.
__pycache__/
# The non-Rust SDKs' own build output: mix's, javac's (sdk/conform-all.sh
# compiles into build/), maven's, and dotnet's.
/sdk/elixir/_build/
/sdk/elixir/deps/
/sdk/java/build/
/sdk/java/target/
/sdk/dotnet/**/bin/
/sdk/dotnet/**/obj/

### reaper ###
# reaper pulls session results into out/ at the tree root.
/out/

### Operating systems ###
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

### Editors ###
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#
.\#*
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

### Local tooling ###
# Claude Code local (per-machine) settings.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Test scratch and generic temp/backups.
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
nohup.out

# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   proto/cabal.project.freeze -- the freeze IS the reproducibility pin.
#   Cargo.lock (Phase 1 on)    -- rue ships binaries; the lock is source.
#   *.patch                    -- tools/rediscovery/patches are the battery.
#   *.log in general           -- fixtures may be logs.
